{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "LUK",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then drew near to him all the publicans and sinners to hear him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Pharisees and scribes murmured, saying, This man receiveth sinners, and eateth with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he spoke this parable to them, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What man of you having a hundred sheep, if he loseth one of them, doth not leave the ninety and nine in the wilderness, and go after that which is lost, until he findeth it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he hath found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he layeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on his shoulders, rejoicing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he cometh home, he calleth together ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " friends and neighbors, saying to them, Rejoice with me; for I have found my sheep which was lost.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I say to you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, who need no repentance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Either what woman having ten pieces of silver, if she loseth one piece, doth not light a candle, and sweep the house, and seek diligently till she findeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when she hath found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", she calleth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " friends and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " neighbors together, saying, Rejoice with me; for I have found the piece which I had lost.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Likewise, I say to you, There is joy in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner that repenteth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, A certain man had two sons:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the younger of them said to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " father, Father, give me the portion of goods that falleth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". And he divided to them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And not many days after, the younger son gathered all together, and took his journey into a far country, and there wasted his substance with riotous living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had spent all, there arose a severe famine in that land; and he began to be in want.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he went and joined himself to a citizen of that country; and he sent him into his fields to feed swine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he would fain have filled his belly with the husks that the swine did eat; and no man gave to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he came to himself, he said, How many hired servants of my father have bread enough and to spare, and I am perishing with hunger!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will arise and go to my father, and will say to him, Father, I have sinned against heaven, and before thee,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And am no more worthy to be called thy son: make me as one of thy hired servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he arose, and came to his father. But when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and had compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the son said to him, Father, I have sinned against heaven, and in thy sight, and am no more worthy to be called thy son.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the father said to his servants, Bring forth the best robe, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on him, and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feet:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And bring hither the fatted calf, and kill ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; and let us eat, and be merry:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this my son was dead, and is alive again; he was lost, and is found. And they began to be merry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now his elder son was in the field: and as he came and drew nigh to the house, he heard music and dancing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he called one of the servants, and asked what these things meant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to him, Thy brother is come; and thy father hath killed the fatted calf, because he hath received him in health.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he was angry, and would not go in; therefore his father came out, and entreated him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he answering, said to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " father, Lo, these many years do I serve thee, neither have I at any time transgressed thy commandment; and yet thou never gavest me a kid, that I might make merry with my friends:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But as soon as this thy son had come, who hath devoured thy living with harlots, thou hast killed for him the fatted calf.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to him, Son, thou art ever with me: and all that I have is thine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LUK.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:LUK.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It was meet that we should make merry, and be glad: for this thy brother was dead, and is alive again; and was lost, and is found.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
